@table(widths=equal)
@row
@cell
@b{Step}

A value that holds and then jumps — rates, counts, state changes.

@graph(type=step, x=week, y=price, title="Posted price")
@data
week,price
1,4.00
2,4.00
3,4.50
4,4.50
5,5.25
@end

@code(idoc)
@graph(type=step, x=week, y=price, title="Posted price")
@data
week,price
1,4.00
2,4.00
3,4.50
4,4.50
5,5.25
@end
@end
@endcell
@cell
@b{Candlestick}

Open/high/low/close per period — a financial series.

@graph(type=candlestick, x=date, title="Daily range")
@data
date,open,high,low,close
2026-01-02,186.4,189.1,185.2,188.6
2026-01-05,188.6,190.2,187.0,187.4
2026-01-06,187.4,188.0,183.5,184.1
2026-01-07,184.1,186.9,183.8,186.5
2026-01-08,186.5,191.3,186.2,190.8
2026-01-09,190.8,192.0,188.4,189.2
@end

@code(idoc)
@graph(type=candlestick, x=date, title="Daily range")
@data
date,open,high,low,close
2026-01-02,186.4,189.1,185.2,188.6
2026-01-05,188.6,190.2,187.0,187.4
2026-01-06,187.4,188.0,183.5,184.1
2026-01-07,184.1,186.9,183.8,186.5
2026-01-08,186.5,191.3,186.2,190.8
2026-01-09,190.8,192.0,188.4,189.2
@end
@end

Finds open/high/low/close by name, and sorts oldest-first — so a file exported newest-first still reads left to right.
@endcell
@endtable

